Dhanvantari
legendary founder of the Āyurveda; ref. to in Bhaviṣyapurāṇa (III. 4. 9); physician to Gods; produced a. the churning of the ocean with a cup of Amṛta in his hands; in a later existence he is called Divodāsa, King of Kāśī. Ref. to in Mahābhārata, Suśruta etc.;
See AIOC. Summaries XXVII. p. 324.
